  "reason": "The evidence strongly favors scvi_n200 + multiprofile + multimodal as the best-performing family, with config_039 (imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) at 0.7250 as the current best. The only remaining untested configuration within this top family is config_027 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted). While avgpool has underperformed transformer for scvi_n200 (config_004: 0.7062 vs config_039: 0.7250), and resnet50 has been slightly weaker than imagenet_vit_l in accuracy (config_013: 0.7131), the weighted fusion consistently helps and resnet50 showed the highest F1 (0.6945) in the set, suggesting complementary discriminative strength. As the final experiment, config_027 completes the scvi_n200 multimodal multiprofile grid, provides the last opportunity to potentially exceed 0.7250 within the most promising design space, and confirms whether the imagenet_vit_l + transformer combination is truly optimal or whether a different pairing could marginally improve performance. All other untested configs involve scgpt, pca_n2000, singleprofile, or unimodal settings, all of which have shown substantially lower performance."
